With some motivation from #nethack, I've compiled a collection of some of
my more interesting side patches and some of the better third party patches
into one large variant, which was quickly dubbed GruntHack.  It's now
reached a point where I'd like to have large scale testing done, so I'm
announcing the release of an alpha (of sorts) of GruntHack 0.1.0.

There are a large number of changes between this and vanilla 3.4.3, so I'll
defer the list to the changes file, which is available as well.  (Pasi
pointed out that a variant of the "while helpless" patch was implemented
but not credited in the documentation, so I'll note that here as well.)

The diff is quite large and cumbersome, so I've elected to release a source
tarball as well.  jmr from #nethack was also kind enough to compile a
win32 binary, which is also available.

All of the above can be found at
http://www.ece.ualberta.ca/~sjm11/grunthack/

I make no guarantees that this code will even compile on any platform
(even the two platforms for which I've known it to compile), but you're
welcome to try.

Please note that this is very early code!  With time and effort, however,
I can envision this becoming a full grown fork, so suggestions and bug
reports are welcome.

Enjoy!


